{"name":"Pepperberry","hex":"#c79d9b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pepperberry","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large Australian laurel, of species Cryptocarya obovata.","Edible fruit of this tree, a black globular drupe."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pepperberry"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cryptocarya obovata","blocks":[{"text":"Cryptocarya obovata, commonly known as pepperberry, white walnut, long tom, she beech or purple laurel, is a species of flowering plant in the laurel family and is endemic to eastern Australia. It is a rainforest tree with oblong to egg-shaped leaves, the flowers creamy-green, tube-shaped and unpleasantly perfumed, and the fruit a spherical drupe with white or cream-coloured cotyledons."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Cryptocarya_obovata_-_RGB_Farm_Cove.JPG/330px-Cryptocarya_obovata_-_RGB_Farm_Cove.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cryptocarya_obovata","wikidata":"Q975756"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Cryptocarya_obovata00.jpg/120px-Cryptocarya_obovata00.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Cryptocarya_obovata00.jpg/250px-Cryptocarya_obovata00.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Cryptocarya_obovata00.jpg/120px-Cryptocarya_obovata00.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACryptocarya_obovata00.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Cryptocarya_obovata_trunk_%26_leaves.JPG/120px-Cryptocarya_obovata_trunk_%26_leaves.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://t